<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 10.44 bln levs of 1-wk, 4-wk T-bill.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 10.44 bln levs of 1-wk, 4-wk T-bill.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry sold on Friday two discount T-bill issues with maturities of one week and four weeks, yielding 3.64 percent and 17.52 percent to maturity, respectively, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Bids were received for a total 10.851 billion levs of T-bills, but the ministry approved bids for only 10.441 billion levs worth.</p>
<p>Details of the issues follow:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG 3012297001     BG3012397009</p>
<p> Term			    one week	     four weeks</p>
<p> Auction date		  January 24, 1997   January 24, 1997</p>
<p> Issue date		    January 24, 1997   January 24, 1997</p>
<p> Maturity date		 January 31, 1997   February 21, 1997</p>
<p> Bids received		 6,503 million levs 4,348.4 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   96.48 pct	    85.07 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		 6,453 million levs 3,988.4 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  96.49 pct	    85.09 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity	3.64 pct	    17.52 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
